1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,241
Sweetheart, on a December night in nineteen

2
00:00:03,241 --> 00:00:05,879
ninety-one, I was stranded at a bus

3
00:00:05,879 --> 00:00:08,291
stop in Mansfield with no purse,

4
00:00:08,291 --> 00:00:10,251
no money, and no way home.

5
00:00:10,431 --> 00:00:12,660
And a little girl about seven,

6
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,739
in a coat two sizes too big,

7
00:00:14,739 --> 00:00:17,488
walked over and pressed a dollar bill

8
00:00:17,488 --> 00:00:18,454
into my hand.

9
00:00:18,634 --> 00:00:19,946
Her only dollar.

10
00:00:20,126 --> 00:00:21,437
Her Christmas money.

11
00:00:21,617 --> 00:00:24,241
I gave her something back that night.

12
00:00:24,421 --> 00:00:26,302
And thirty-one years later,

13
00:00:26,302 --> 00:00:27,347
I saw it again,

14
00:00:27,347 --> 00:00:29,298
pinned to a nurse's uniform.

15
00:00:29,647 --> 00:00:31,950
Tonight I'm going to tell you what

16
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,576
I gave that little girl,

17
00:00:33,576 --> 00:00:35,744
and the night in a hospital room

18
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:37,572
in two thousand twenty-two,

19
00:00:37,572 --> 00:00:40,214
when I was seventy-eight and very sick,

20
00:00:40,214 --> 00:00:42,246
and a nurse leaned over my bed

21
00:00:42,246 --> 00:00:44,752
and said six words I'll never forget.

22
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:46,124
Stay with me,

23
00:00:46,124 --> 00:00:46,674
honey.

24
00:00:47,023 --> 00:00:49,541
It was the Friday before Christmas,

25
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:49,972
honey.

26
00:00:50,152 --> 00:00:52,765
I'd gone downtown after work to buy

27
00:00:52,765 --> 00:00:55,377
Harold's present, a new wristwatch,

28
00:00:55,377 --> 00:00:57,915
and I'd spent the afternoon in the

29
00:00:57,915 --> 00:00:59,557
stores on Main Street.

30
00:00:59,737 --> 00:01:02,666
And somewhere between the jewelry counter and

31
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:03,708
the parking lot,

32
00:01:03,708 --> 00:01:05,791
my purse was stolen right off my

33
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:06,377
shoulder.

34
00:01:06,557 --> 00:01:08,263
Wallet, car keys,

35
00:01:08,263 --> 00:01:09,367
everything.

36
00:01:09,547 --> 00:01:11,586
And when I got to my car,

37
00:01:11,586 --> 00:01:13,053
I couldn't get in.

38
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:14,340
It was dark,

39
00:01:14,340 --> 00:01:16,739
and it was eleven degrees.

40
00:01:17,089 --> 00:01:19,307
This was before cell phones,

41
00:01:19,307 --> 00:01:20,178
sweetheart.

42
00:01:20,358 --> 00:01:22,438
I didn't have a quarter for the

43
00:01:22,438 --> 00:01:23,109
pay phone.

44
00:01:23,289 --> 00:01:25,138
I went back to the stores,

45
00:01:25,138 --> 00:01:26,703
but they were closing.

46
00:01:26,883 --> 00:01:28,877
So I walked to the bus stop

47
00:01:28,877 --> 00:01:30,133
on Fourth Street,

48
00:01:30,133 --> 00:01:32,645
thinking I could beg the driver to

49
00:01:32,645 --> 00:01:33,384
let me on.

50
00:01:33,564 --> 00:01:34,908
The sign said,

51
00:01:34,908 --> 00:01:37,117
exact fare, one dollar.

52
00:01:37,297 --> 00:01:39,132
And when the bus came,

53
00:01:39,132 --> 00:01:42,052
the driver shook his head and said,

54
00:01:42,052 --> 00:01:43,137
sorry, ma'am.

55
00:01:43,317 --> 00:01:44,257
Rules.

56
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,051
And he drove away.

57
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:48,715
The next bus wasn't for an hour.

58
00:01:49,065 --> 00:01:51,274
I sat down on that cold bench,

59
00:01:51,274 --> 00:01:52,893
forty-seven years old,

60
00:01:52,893 --> 00:01:55,176
and I'm not ashamed to tell you

61
00:01:55,176 --> 00:01:55,764
I cried.

62
00:01:55,944 --> 00:01:57,605
My feet were numb.

63
00:01:57,785 --> 00:01:59,236
My hands were numb.

64
00:01:59,416 --> 00:02:00,898
And across the street,

65
00:02:00,898 --> 00:02:03,459
there was a little laundromat with the

66
00:02:03,459 --> 00:02:05,683
lights on, and inside I could see

67
00:02:05,683 --> 00:02:07,771
a young mother folding clothes,

68
00:02:07,771 --> 00:02:09,928
and a little girl sitting on the

69
00:02:09,928 --> 00:02:13,162
washing machine, watching me through the window.

70
00:02:13,342 --> 00:02:15,241
In a minute I'll tell you what

71
00:02:15,241 --> 00:02:16,570
that little girl did.

72
00:02:16,919 --> 00:02:19,444
She came out the door and crossed

73
00:02:19,444 --> 00:02:21,203
that street by herself,

74
00:02:21,203 --> 00:02:23,804
honey, in a man's winter coat that

75
00:02:23,804 --> 00:02:25,716
came down past her knees,

76
00:02:25,716 --> 00:02:28,622
with the sleeves rolled up four times.

77
00:02:28,802 --> 00:02:30,885
Tennis shoes, no boots,

78
00:02:30,885 --> 00:02:31,972
in the snow.

79
00:02:32,152 --> 00:02:33,638
Her nose was running.

80
00:02:33,818 --> 00:02:36,141
She walked right up to me and

81
00:02:36,141 --> 00:02:38,624
said, lady, why are you crying?

82
00:02:38,804 --> 00:02:39,859
And I said,

83
00:02:39,859 --> 00:02:43,119
oh, honey, somebody took my purse,

84
00:02:43,119 --> 00:02:45,132
and I can't get home.

85
00:02:45,481 --> 00:02:47,616
And she reached into the pocket of

86
00:02:47,616 --> 00:02:49,500
that big coat and pulled out a

87
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:50,253
dollar bill.

88
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:52,613
It was folded up very small,

89
00:02:52,613 --> 00:02:54,248
into a little square,

90
00:02:54,248 --> 00:02:57,597
the way children fold money they're saving.

91
00:02:57,777 --> 00:02:59,345
And she said,

92
00:02:59,345 --> 00:02:59,948
here.

93
00:03:00,128 --> 00:03:01,892
You can take the bus.

94
00:03:02,072 --> 00:03:03,409
And I said,

95
00:03:03,409 --> 00:03:05,718
oh, sweetheart, no.

96
00:03:05,898 --> 00:03:07,140
That's your money.

97
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,311
And she said,

98
00:03:08,311 --> 00:03:10,977
it's my Christmas money for my mom.

99
00:03:11,157 --> 00:03:12,574
But you need it more.

100
00:03:12,754 --> 00:03:14,147
She's not crying.

101
00:03:14,497 --> 00:03:17,928
If Grandma's story is touching your heart,

102
00:03:17,928 --> 00:03:20,134
tap the like button for me,

103
00:03:20,134 --> 00:03:21,033
sweetheart.

104
00:03:21,213 --> 00:03:24,452
It helps more people find these stories.

105
00:03:24,632 --> 00:03:26,464
I looked across the street,

106
00:03:26,464 --> 00:03:28,772
and her mother was standing in the

107
00:03:28,772 --> 00:03:30,739
laundromat doorway, watching,

108
00:03:30,739 --> 00:03:33,386
with her arms crossed against the cold.

109
00:03:33,566 --> 00:03:35,308
And she nodded at me.

110
00:03:35,488 --> 00:03:36,765
Just once.

111
00:03:36,945 --> 00:03:37,955
Go ahead.

112
00:03:38,135 --> 00:03:40,405
That mother didn't have much,

113
00:03:40,405 --> 00:03:40,875
honey.

114
00:03:41,055 --> 00:03:42,297
You could see it.

115
00:03:42,477 --> 00:03:44,411
But she let her daughter give it

116
00:03:44,411 --> 00:03:44,834
anyway.

117
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:46,831
I took that dollar,

118
00:03:46,831 --> 00:03:47,784
sweetheart.

119
00:03:47,964 --> 00:03:50,226
I took it because she needed me

120
00:03:50,226 --> 00:03:51,029
to take it.

121
00:03:51,209 --> 00:03:53,984
You can't refuse a gift like that.

122
00:03:54,164 --> 00:03:56,451
But I wanted to give her something

123
00:03:56,451 --> 00:03:58,065
back, and I had nothing.

124
00:03:58,245 --> 00:04:00,277
No purse, no money.

125
00:04:00,457 --> 00:04:01,622
Then I felt it,

126
00:04:01,622 --> 00:04:03,487
on the lapel of my coat.

127
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:05,702
A little silver angel pin,

128
00:04:05,702 --> 00:04:07,972
with a tiny blue stone in the

129
00:04:07,972 --> 00:04:08,520
middle.

130
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,465
My mother had given it to me

131
00:04:10,465 --> 00:04:12,357
the Christmas before she died.

132
00:04:12,706 --> 00:04:16,088
My mother had passed in nineteen eighty-nine,

133
00:04:16,088 --> 00:04:18,268
honey, just two years before.

134
00:04:18,448 --> 00:04:20,908
And that pin was the last gift

135
00:04:20,908 --> 00:04:22,302
she ever gave me.

136
00:04:22,482 --> 00:04:24,665
I'd worn it every day since.

137
00:04:24,845 --> 00:04:26,568
And I took it off my coat

138
00:04:26,568 --> 00:04:28,981
and pinned it on that little girl's

139
00:04:28,981 --> 00:04:31,463
enormous coat, right over her heart.

140
00:04:31,643 --> 00:04:32,583
And I said,

141
00:04:32,583 --> 00:04:34,719
this is a guardian angel.

142
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:36,234
She watched over me.

143
00:04:36,414 --> 00:04:38,864
Now she's going to watch over you.

144
00:04:39,044 --> 00:04:40,408
What's your name,

145
00:04:40,408 --> 00:04:40,890
honey?

146
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:43,074
She said, Tasha.

147
00:04:43,254 --> 00:04:45,096
And then the bus came,

148
00:04:45,096 --> 00:04:46,435
and I had to go.

149
00:04:46,615 --> 00:04:48,369
I got on with her dollar,

150
00:04:48,369 --> 00:04:50,052
and I sat at the window,

151
00:04:50,052 --> 00:04:52,787
and I watched that little girl standing

152
00:04:52,787 --> 00:04:54,751
at the bus stop in her giant

153
00:04:54,751 --> 00:04:57,347
coat, touching the angel pin with one

154
00:04:57,347 --> 00:05:00,152
finger, until the bus turned the corner.

155
00:05:00,332 --> 00:05:02,760
I told Harold the whole story that

156
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:03,188
night.

157
00:05:03,368 --> 00:05:05,772
He held me while I cried.

158
00:05:05,952 --> 00:05:07,325
And then he said,

159
00:05:07,325 --> 00:05:09,667
Ruthie, you'll see her again.

160
00:05:10,017 --> 00:05:11,917
When I got home that night,

161
00:05:11,917 --> 00:05:14,522
Harold had to break a basement window

162
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:15,437
to let us in,

163
00:05:15,437 --> 00:05:17,760
because my house keys were in the

164
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:18,956
stolen purse too.

165
00:05:19,136 --> 00:05:21,098
He didn't care one bit.

166
00:05:21,278 --> 00:05:23,574
He wrapped me in the afghan off

167
00:05:23,574 --> 00:05:25,574
the couch, made me a cup of

168
00:05:25,574 --> 00:05:27,796
cocoa, and sat my numb feet in

169
00:05:27,796 --> 00:05:29,278
a pan of warm water.

170
00:05:29,458 --> 00:05:32,162
And while I told him about Tasha,

171
00:05:32,162 --> 00:05:33,718
I watched his face.

172
00:05:33,898 --> 00:05:35,908
I'll tell you what my Harold did

173
00:05:35,908 --> 00:05:37,730
the next morning in a minute.

174
00:05:38,079 --> 00:05:41,330
He drove downtown first thing and talked

175
00:05:41,330 --> 00:05:42,874
to the bus company,

176
00:05:42,874 --> 00:05:43,362
honey.

177
00:05:43,542 --> 00:05:45,813
He told them the whole story,

178
00:05:45,813 --> 00:05:47,223
and he asked them,

179
00:05:47,223 --> 00:05:48,163
from now on,

180
00:05:48,163 --> 00:05:51,061
to let anybody ride free on Christmas

181
00:05:51,061 --> 00:05:52,784
week who couldn't pay.

182
00:05:52,964 --> 00:05:54,322
They said no.

183
00:05:54,502 --> 00:05:55,500
Rules.

184
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:57,876
So every December after that,

185
00:05:57,876 --> 00:05:59,390
for seventeen years,

186
00:05:59,390 --> 00:06:00,601
until he passed,

187
00:06:00,601 --> 00:06:03,175
Harold left a roll of dollar bills

188
00:06:03,175 --> 00:06:05,976
with the drivers at the Fourth Street

189
00:06:05,976 --> 00:06:08,475
depot, for whoever came up short.

190
00:06:08,655 --> 00:06:11,290
He never told anybody but me.

191
00:06:11,639 --> 00:06:13,845
I went back to that laundromat,

192
00:06:13,845 --> 00:06:15,979
honey, the very next Saturday,

193
00:06:15,979 --> 00:06:18,042
with a box of groceries and a

194
00:06:18,042 --> 00:06:20,034
Christmas present for Tasha.

195
00:06:20,214 --> 00:06:22,066
A real winter coat,

196
00:06:22,066 --> 00:06:23,237
in her size,

197
00:06:23,237 --> 00:06:24,602
and red boots.

198
00:06:24,782 --> 00:06:26,768
But the woman at the counter said

199
00:06:26,768 --> 00:06:28,814
the young mother and her girl only

200
00:06:28,814 --> 00:06:30,258
came in once in a while,

201
00:06:30,258 --> 00:06:32,304
and she didn't know their names or

202
00:06:32,304 --> 00:06:33,327
where they lived.

203
00:06:33,507 --> 00:06:35,446
I left the box with her.

204
00:06:35,626 --> 00:06:37,362
I don't know if they ever got

205
00:06:37,362 --> 00:06:37,542
it.

206
00:06:37,722 --> 00:06:40,009
I went back four more times.

207
00:06:40,189 --> 00:06:42,011
I never saw them again.

208
00:06:42,361 --> 00:06:44,440
So far, the stolen purse,

209
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:46,685
the bus that wouldn't wait,

210
00:06:46,685 --> 00:06:49,180
a little girl's folded dollar,

211
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:51,591
and my mother's silver angel.

212
00:06:51,771 --> 00:06:53,441
I kept that dollar,

213
00:06:53,441 --> 00:06:54,407
sweetheart.

214
00:06:54,587 --> 00:06:56,143
I never spent it.

215
00:06:56,323 --> 00:06:58,220
I put it in a little frame,

216
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:00,257
and it hung in my kitchen for

217
00:07:00,257 --> 00:07:03,138
thirty years, right next to the calendar.

218
00:07:03,318 --> 00:07:05,574
Every time I looked at it,

219
00:07:05,574 --> 00:07:08,437
I said a little prayer for Tasha,

220
00:07:08,437 --> 00:07:09,912
wherever she was.

221
00:07:10,092 --> 00:07:11,096
Stay with me,

222
00:07:11,096 --> 00:07:12,948
because then I got sick.

223
00:07:13,299 --> 00:07:16,513
In February of two thousand twenty-two,

224
00:07:16,513 --> 00:07:17,831
I got pneumonia,

225
00:07:17,831 --> 00:07:18,326
honey.

226
00:07:18,506 --> 00:07:19,225
Bad.

227
00:07:19,405 --> 00:07:20,846
I was seventy-eight,

228
00:07:20,846 --> 00:07:22,503
and my lungs were full,

229
00:07:22,503 --> 00:07:24,809
and they took me to the hospital

230
00:07:24,809 --> 00:07:27,114
in an ambulance in the middle of

231
00:07:27,114 --> 00:07:27,834
the night.

232
00:07:28,014 --> 00:07:30,429
Susan flew in from Arizona.

233
00:07:30,609 --> 00:07:32,884
Mark slept in a chair by my

234
00:07:32,884 --> 00:07:33,221
bed.

235
00:07:33,401 --> 00:07:34,390
For three days,

236
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:36,763
the doctors weren't sure I was going

237
00:07:36,763 --> 00:07:37,488
to make it.

238
00:07:37,668 --> 00:07:40,441
I don't remember much of those three

239
00:07:40,441 --> 00:07:40,826
days.

240
00:07:41,176 --> 00:07:43,126
But I remember the fourth night.

241
00:07:43,306 --> 00:07:45,156
I woke up at two in the

242
00:07:45,156 --> 00:07:47,650
morning, and the room was dark,

243
00:07:47,650 --> 00:07:49,018
and I was scared.

244
00:07:49,198 --> 00:07:51,508
And a nurse came in to check

245
00:07:51,508 --> 00:07:52,333
my oxygen.

246
00:07:52,513 --> 00:07:53,636
A tall woman,

247
00:07:53,636 --> 00:07:57,351
about thirty-eight, with her hair in braids

248
00:07:57,351 --> 00:07:58,734
and the kindest,

249
00:07:58,734 --> 00:07:59,943
calmest voice.

250
00:08:00,123 --> 00:08:02,374
She held my hand and said,

251
00:08:02,374 --> 00:08:05,057
Miss Ruth, you're doing better.

252
00:08:05,237 --> 00:08:06,874
Your numbers are good.

253
00:08:07,054 --> 00:08:08,843
And I looked up at her,

254
00:08:08,843 --> 00:08:11,177
honey, and on her blue scrubs,

255
00:08:11,177 --> 00:08:12,810
right over her heart,

256
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:15,610
there was a little silver angel with

257
00:08:15,610 --> 00:08:16,621
a blue stone.

258
00:08:16,971 --> 00:08:19,072
I couldn't talk very well,

259
00:08:19,072 --> 00:08:21,255
because of the oxygen mask.

260
00:08:21,435 --> 00:08:23,735
But I reached up with my hand,

261
00:08:23,735 --> 00:08:25,498
and I touched that pin.

262
00:08:25,678 --> 00:08:27,930
And she looked down at it,

263
00:08:27,930 --> 00:08:29,229
and she smiled,

264
00:08:29,229 --> 00:08:30,355
and she said,

265
00:08:30,355 --> 00:08:31,135
oh, this?

266
00:08:31,315 --> 00:08:33,401
Somebody gave this to me when I

267
00:08:33,401 --> 00:08:34,612
was a little girl.

268
00:08:34,792 --> 00:08:36,766
A lady at a bus stop.

269
00:08:36,946 --> 00:08:39,525
And I pulled the mask down,

270
00:08:39,525 --> 00:08:40,575
and I said,

271
00:08:40,575 --> 00:08:41,149
Tasha?

272
00:08:41,329 --> 00:08:42,674
And she froze,

273
00:08:42,674 --> 00:08:43,732
sweetheart.

274
00:08:43,912 --> 00:08:45,363
She just froze.

275
00:08:45,713 --> 00:08:47,291
She looked at my chart.

276
00:08:47,471 --> 00:08:48,249
Ruth.

277
00:08:48,429 --> 00:08:50,204
She looked at my face,

278
00:08:50,204 --> 00:08:51,494
for a long time.

279
00:08:51,674 --> 00:08:54,031
And then she said six words.

280
00:08:54,211 --> 00:08:56,847
She said, I prayed I'd find you.

281
00:08:57,027 --> 00:08:58,973
And she sat down on the edge

282
00:08:58,973 --> 00:08:59,668
of my bed,

283
00:08:59,668 --> 00:09:01,197
at two in the morning,

284
00:09:01,197 --> 00:09:03,282
and we both cried so hard that

285
00:09:03,282 --> 00:09:05,715
the other nurse came running to see

286
00:09:05,715 --> 00:09:07,592
if my monitors were broken.

287
00:09:07,941 --> 00:09:10,853
Tasha told me everything over the next

288
00:09:10,853 --> 00:09:12,922
week, honey, on her breaks.

289
00:09:13,102 --> 00:09:15,831
Her mother had been raising her alone,

290
00:09:15,831 --> 00:09:17,052
working two jobs,

291
00:09:17,052 --> 00:09:19,566
and they'd been living in a shelter

292
00:09:19,566 --> 00:09:20,428
that winter.

293
00:09:20,608 --> 00:09:23,197
That's why they used the laundromat.

294
00:09:23,377 --> 00:09:25,587
They moved to Akron in the new

295
00:09:25,587 --> 00:09:28,091
year, before they ever got my box.

296
00:09:28,271 --> 00:09:30,403
And her mother had told her,

297
00:09:30,403 --> 00:09:32,460
every Christmas after that,

298
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:35,582
that angel pin means somebody believed in

299
00:09:35,582 --> 00:09:35,887
you.

300
00:09:36,067 --> 00:09:37,646
Don't you ever forget it.

301
00:09:37,996 --> 00:09:40,194
She'd worn that pin on her coat

302
00:09:40,194 --> 00:09:41,967
all through grade school,

303
00:09:41,967 --> 00:09:44,449
sweetheart, and on her dress at her

304
00:09:44,449 --> 00:09:46,081
high school graduation,

305
00:09:46,081 --> 00:09:47,783
the first in her family.

306
00:09:47,963 --> 00:09:50,023
She wore it under her gown when

307
00:09:50,023 --> 00:09:51,817
she got her nursing degree.

308
00:09:51,997 --> 00:09:54,379
And she'd pinned it on her scrubs

309
00:09:54,379 --> 00:09:56,978
every single shift for twelve years.

310
00:09:57,158 --> 00:09:59,747
She said, every scared patient I hold

311
00:09:59,747 --> 00:10:02,056
hands with at two in the morning,

312
00:10:02,056 --> 00:10:04,435
I'm thinking about the lady at the

313
00:10:04,435 --> 00:10:05,064
bus stop.

314
00:10:05,415 --> 00:10:08,133
When I went home from the hospital,

315
00:10:08,133 --> 00:10:10,541
Tasha came to my house on Maple

316
00:10:10,541 --> 00:10:12,871
Drive and saw her dollar bill,

317
00:10:12,871 --> 00:10:15,512
still folded in its little square,

318
00:10:15,512 --> 00:10:17,686
in the frame by my calendar.

319
00:10:17,866 --> 00:10:19,492
Thirty-one years.

320
00:10:19,672 --> 00:10:21,854
She put her hand on the glass.

321
00:10:22,034 --> 00:10:23,094
And she said,

322
00:10:23,094 --> 00:10:25,541
Miss Ruth, you never spent it.

323
00:10:25,721 --> 00:10:27,190
I said, honey,

324
00:10:27,190 --> 00:10:28,449
how could I?

325
00:10:28,629 --> 00:10:31,912
It was the most valuable dollar anybody

326
00:10:31,912 --> 00:10:33,006
ever gave me.

327
00:10:33,186 --> 00:10:34,649
It got me home.

328
00:10:34,999 --> 00:10:37,672
Tasha and her mother came to Christmas

329
00:10:37,672 --> 00:10:38,868
dinner that year,

330
00:10:38,868 --> 00:10:39,642
sweetheart.

331
00:10:39,822 --> 00:10:41,262
Her mother, Denise,

332
00:10:41,262 --> 00:10:43,307
is about my daughter's age,

333
00:10:43,307 --> 00:10:45,579
and the two of them talked all

334
00:10:45,579 --> 00:10:46,034
night.

335
00:10:46,214 --> 00:10:48,285
Tasha has a little girl of her

336
00:10:48,285 --> 00:10:50,010
own now, eight years old.

337
00:10:50,190 --> 00:10:52,438
And on Christmas Eve last year,

338
00:10:52,438 --> 00:10:54,758
Tasha took the angel pin off her

339
00:10:54,758 --> 00:10:57,006
own scrubs and pinned it on her

340
00:10:57,006 --> 00:10:58,166
daughter's coat.

341
00:10:58,346 --> 00:11:00,541
And she told her the whole story.

342
00:11:00,721 --> 00:11:01,765
The bus stop,

343
00:11:01,765 --> 00:11:04,575
the dollar, and the lady who cried.

344
00:11:04,925 --> 00:11:07,453
Here's what I want you to remember,

345
00:11:07,453 --> 00:11:07,886
honey.

346
00:11:08,066 --> 00:11:10,458
There's no such thing as a small

347
00:11:10,458 --> 00:11:11,131
kindness.

348
00:11:11,311 --> 00:11:12,554
A dollar, a pin,

349
00:11:12,554 --> 00:11:14,419
a hand to hold at two in

350
00:11:14,419 --> 00:11:15,351
the morning.

351
00:11:15,531 --> 00:11:17,880
You never know where it's going to

352
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:18,225
land.

353
00:11:18,405 --> 00:11:20,120
Tell me in the comments,

354
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:23,194
sweetheart, has a child ever done something

355
00:11:23,194 --> 00:11:25,696
kind for you that you never forgot?

356
00:11:25,876 --> 00:11:28,154
There are more of my family's stories

357
00:11:28,154 --> 00:11:30,309
in the playlist right there on your

358
00:11:30,309 --> 00:11:30,740
screen.

359
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:31,710
Good night.

360
00:11:31,890 --> 00:11:33,318
Merry Christmas.
